I have been surprised at all the Sys V problems - We have a Vax 8600
running ordinary System V Rel 2.0 and it took me all of about 30 minutes
to get nethack 2.2 running. I had absolutely no trouble using curses
except for ospeed being undeclared in termcap.c (or tty.c I don't
remember). The only other problem I had was an incorrect #define for
rand() in rnd.c.

I used Makefile.unix, changed termlib to curses and made the appropriate
changes to config.h.

Well, what else can I say, I guess not all Sys V systems are equal.


